pokebw2-pointers3.patch (tools/pokebw2_fetch.sh, the maintainers' notes): more u32s that carry a pointer, pointer-wide
(uintptr_t), after pokebw2-pointers.patch and pokebw2-pointers2.patch; found by the int-to-pointer scan in the maintainers' notes.
A 64-bit pointer passed through a u32 loses its top half and the cast back faults. The values that are not pointers
are the same zero-extended, so the DS build's code is the same.
- the C-Gear beacon view's wait events (src/ov084/beacon_view_setup.c: the menu button passed as the event's param)
  and the Entralink mission view's (src/ov085/fmission_view_setup.c, the same);
- the beacon mission's value (src/system/game_beacon.c GameBeaconSendSlot_SetMission/Ex: a name StrBuf for 0x67);
- the Union Room's self state (src/ov028/union_comm.c UnionComm_SetSelf: the target beacon entry);
- the Pokestar Studios movie field (src/system/pokewood_rec.c Pokewood_GetLoadedMovieField: the PartyPkm to fill).

